	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/markdown" rect="(22.0, 5.0, 158.0, 54.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">**EDA = Explorative Data Analysis**</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(703.0, 198.0, 201.0, 75.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">works on single column</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/plain" rect="(702.0, 305.0, 239.0, 54.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">works on a single column</text>
		<text id="3" type="text/plain" rect="(699.0, 427.0, 249.0, 33.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">works on 2+ columns</text>
		<arrow id="4" start="(510.0, 807.0)" end="(435.0, 802.0)" fill="#C1272D" />
		<text id="5" type="text/plain" rect="(535.0, 774.0, 293.0, 138.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">it displays the correlation matrix by pressing the RUN button on the bottom-left hand corner</text>
		<text id="6" type="text/markdown" rect="(-163.0, 772.0, 264.0, 201.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">An example of **positive** correlation (from 0 to 1): between the price and the square meters of an apartment.
An example of **negative** correlation (from 0 to -1): between the price and the kilometers of an used car. The threshold for importance of correlationis |0.7|</text>
		<arrow id="7" start="(114.0, 826.0)" end="(211.0, 805.0)" fill="#C1272D" />
		<text id="8" type="text/plain" rect="(149.0, 879.0, 292.0, 61.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">In EDA all columns play the same role; there are NOT targets and predictors</text>
	</annotations>
